# Frontend UX Modernization

Authority: `docs/ui_design_system.md` (subordinate to architecture rules).

Stack: **Blade + Tailwind + Alpine only** — no React, Vue, or new JS frameworks.

## Design Philosophy

Dense internal SaaS for multi-branch dental lab operations. Operational, not promotional. Status always visible. Branch- and permission-truthful. Honest empty states. Reuse before reinvention.

## Layout & Shell

- Render module pages inside `<x-settings-shell>` with permission-aware sidebar
- Canvas: `bg-gray-100`; cards: `rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white shadow-sm`
- Primary color: **teal** (`teal-700`, ring `teal-500`) — indigo is legacy/deprecated
- Font: **Figtree** only (via `tailwind.config.js`)

## Component Families (reuse first)

- `owner-dashboard.*` — owner KPI surfaces
- `branch-dashboard.*` — branch admin surfaces
- `inventory.*` — inventory module (Sprint 12 reference: `inventory/products/index`)
- Breeze form primitives for inputs/buttons

## List & Table Patterns

- Dual layout: desktop table + mobile stacked cards
- `<th scope="col">`, `tabular-nums` for quantities/currency
- Semantic status badges (`_status-badge`, `_low-stock-badge` partials)
- Row tinting for status; never color alone
- Horizontal scroll for dense tables on small screens

## Forms & Actions

- Associated `<label for="...">` on every input
- Visible teal focus rings; keyboard operable
- Permission-aware action buttons (`@can`/`@canany` — never sole protection)
- Destructive flows via `<x-modal>`, not `prompt()`/`alert()`
- UI text: Bahasa Indonesia for operator-facing labels (per migration standard)

## Empty States & Data Honesty

- Every list needs an empty state explaining what is missing
- Never fabricate data; label ledger-derived values as derived
- Selectors show only active-branch records

## Accessibility

- Sufficient contrast, status text + color, focus management
- Sidebar reachable on mobile

## When Touching Legacy Views

Views using indigo accents, `sm:rounded-lg` only, or no mobile layout are **legacy**. Converge to this standard when modified.
